en.\n2009 | \n2010 |         Parameters\n2011 |         ==========\n2012 | \n2013 |         args : Expr\n2014 |             A *rule*, or *pattern* and *rule*.\n2015 |             - *pattern* is a type or an iterable of types.\n2016 |             - *rule* can be any object.\n2017 | \n2018 |         deep : bool, optional\n2019 |             If ``True``, subexpressions are recursively transformed. Default is\n2020 |             ``True``.\n2021 | \n2022 |         Examples\n2023 |         ========\n2024 | \n2025 |         If *pattern* is unspecified, all possible expressions are transformed.\n2026 | \n2027 |         >>> from sympy import cos, sin, exp, I\n2028 |         >>> from sympy.abc import x\n2029 |         >>> expr = cos(x) + I*sin(x)\n2030 |         >>> expr.rewrite(exp)\n2031 |         exp(I*x)\n2032 | \n2033 |         Pattern can be a type or an iterable of types.\n2034 | \n2035 |         >>> expr.rewrite(sin, exp)\n2036 |         exp(I*x)/2 + cos(x) - exp(-I*x)/2\n2037 |         >>> expr.rewrite([cos,], exp)\n2038 |         exp(I*x)/2 + I*sin(x) + exp(-I*x)/2\n2039 |         >>> expr.rewrite([cos, sin], exp)\n2040 |         exp(I*x)\n2041 | \n2042 |         Rewriting behavior can be implemented by defining ``_eval_rewrite()``\n2043 |         method.\n2044 | \n2045 |         >>> from sympy import Expr, sqrt, pi\n2046 |         >>> class MySin(Expr):\n2047 |         ...     def _eval_rewrite(self, rule, args, **hints):\n2048 |         ...         x, = args\n2049 |         ...         if rule == cos:\n2050 |         ...             return cos(pi/2 - x, evaluate=False)\n2051 |         ...         if rule == sqrt:\n2052 |         ...             return sqrt(1 - cos(x)**2)\n2053 |         >>> MySin(MySin(x)).rewrite(cos)\n2054 |         cos(-cos(-x + pi/2) + pi/2)\n2055 |         >>> MySin(x).rewrite(sqrt)\n2056 |         sqrt(1 - cos(x)**2)\n2057 | \n2058 |         Defining ``_eval_rewrite_as_[...]()`` method is supported for backwards\n2059 |         compatibility