    assert_array_almost_equal(rank_proba, rank_score)\n3764 |         except AssertionError:\n3765 |             # Sometimes, the rounding applied on the probabilities will have\n3766 |             # ties that are not present in the scores because it is\n3767 |             # numerically more precise. In this case, we relax the test by\n3768 |             # grouping the decision function scores based on the probability\n3769 |             # rank and check that the score is monotonically increasing.\n3770 |             grouped_y_score = np.array(\n3771 |                 [b[rank_proba == group].mean() for group in np.unique(rank_proba)]\n3772 |             )\n3773 |             sorted_idx = np.argsort(grouped_y_score)\n3774 |             assert_array_equal(sorted_idx, np.arange(len(sorted_idx)))\n```\n\nFound function `sklearn/feature_extraction/_hash.py:FeatureHasher.fit`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n128 | def fit(self, X=None, y=None):\n129 |         \"\"\"Only validates estimator's parameters.\n130 | \n131 |         This method allows to: (i) validate the estimator's parameters and\n132 |         (ii) be consistent with the scikit-learn transformer API.\n133 | \n134 |         Parameters\n135 |         ----------\n136 |         X : Ignored\n137 |             Not used, present here for API consistency by convention.\n138 | \n139 |         y : Ignored\n140 |             Not used, present here for API consistency by convention.\n141 | \n142 |         Returns\n143 |         -------\n144 |         self : object\n145 |             FeatureHasher class instance.\n146 |         \"\"\"\n147 |         return self\n```\n\n\n\n##Searching for term \"docstring consistency\", \"docstring consistency assert consistent docs\"...\n### Search Result:\nFound function `doc/api_reference.py:_get_submodule`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n21 | def _get_submodule(module_name, submodule_name):\n22 |     \"\"\"Get the submodule docstring and automatically add the hook.\n23 | \n24 |     `module_name` is e.g. `sklearn.feature_extraction`, and `submodule_name` is e.g.\n25 |     `image`, so we get the docstring and hook for `sklearn.feature_extraction.image`\n26 |     submodule. `module_name` is used to reset the current module because autosummary\n27 |     automatically changes the current module.\n28 |     \"\"\"\n29 |     lines = [\n30 |         f\".. automodule:: {module_name}.{submodule_name}\",\n31 |         f\".. currentmodule:: {module_name}\",\n32 |     ]\n33 |     return \"\\n\\n\".join(lines)\n```\n\n\n\n##Searching for term \"assert consistent docs\"...\n### Search Result:\nFound .\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n21 | dependent_packages = {\n22 |     \"numpy\": (NUMPY_MIN_VERSION, \"build, install\"),\n23 |     \"scipy\": (SCIPY_MIN_VERSION, \"build, install\"),\n24 |     \"joblib\": (JOBLIB_MIN_VERSION, \"install\"),\n25 |     \"threadpoolctl\": (THREADPOOLCTL_MIN_VERSION, \"install\"),\n26 |     \"cython\": (CYTHON_MIN_VERSION, \"build\"),\n27 |     \"meson-python\": (\"0.16.0\", \"build\"),\n28 |     \"matplotlib\": (\"3.3.4\", \"benchmark, docs, examples, tests\"),\n29 |     \"scikit-image\": (\"0.17.2\", \"docs, examples, tests\"),\n30 |     \"pandas\": (\"1.1.5\", \"benchmark, docs, examples, tests\"),\n31 |     \"seaborn\": (\"0.9.0\", \"docs, examples\"),\n32 |     \"memory_profiler\": (\"0.57.0\", \"benchmark, docs\"),\n33 |     \"pytest\": (PYTEST_MIN_VERSION, \"tests\"),\n34 |     \"pytest-cov\": (\"2.9.0\", \"tests\"),\n35 |     \"ruff\": (\"0.5.1\", \"tests\"),\n36 |     \"black\": (\"24.3.0\", \"tests\"),\n37 |     \"mypy\": (\"1.9\", \"tests\"),\n38 |     \"pyamg\": (\"4.0.0\", \"tests\"),\n39 |     \"polars\": (\"0.20.30\", \"docs, tests\"),\n40 |     \"pyarrow\": (\"12.0.0\", \"tests\"),\n41 |     \"sphinx\": (\"7.3.7\", \"docs\"),\n42 |     \"sphinx-copybutton\": (\"0.5.2\", \"docs\"),\n43 |     \"sphinx-gallery\": (\"0